+## SDK version
+
+The app pins `react-native-purchases` to **10.16.1**, exactly — no caret. This
+is the version Expo SDK 58 (React Native 0.88) can build: EAS builds iOS with
+CocoaPods, and RevenueCat's 11.x release note says to stay on 10.x for Expo apps
+until the `PurchasesHybridCommon` pod and the Swift Package Manager path are in
+place (`12.0.0` requires RN 0.88 with SwiftPM). 10.16.1 is also what npm's
+`hotfix` dist-tag points at. Move to 11/12 as a deliberate migration once the
+iOS build uses SwiftPM and the v11 API changes are applied, not by drifting a
+caret range.
+
 ## App configuration
 
 `app.json` carries version `1.1.0` / iOS build `2` / Android `versionCode 2`.
